    "result_text": "The full suite passes (25 tests, 0 failures) with a green build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field following the existing pattern used by other computed Owner fields (like `membershipNumber`), where a getter on the `Owner` model is auto-mapped by MapStruct into the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field in API responses.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a computed `getMembershipTier()`:\n   ```java\n   public String getMembershipTier() {\n       boolean hasEmail = this.email != null && !this.email.isBlank();\n       if (this.namesakeCount != null && this.namesakeCount == 0 && hasEmail) {\n           return \"SILVER\";\n       }\n       return \"BRONZE\";\n   }\n   ```\n   Returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 **and** an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nBoth new `Cp15Tests` cases (SILVER when unique with email, BRONZE when no email) pass, and all 25 tests in the suite are green.",
